# Findings gitleaks has judged and this repo has judged back.
#
# Fingerprints, deliberately — not a path or rule allowlist. A fingerprint is
# file + rule + LINE, so these entries silence exactly these findings and
# nothing else. A new secret on line 25 of the same file, or a different rule
# firing on the same line, still fails the release. And if one of these lines
# moves, its fingerprint stops matching and the finding comes back for
# re-review rather than staying silently suppressed.
#
# The `/repo/` prefix is not decoration: gitleaks builds the fingerprint from
# the path it was given, and the release script scans a staged copy bind-mounted
# at /repo. Without it these lines match nothing and the gate fails while
# looking configured.
#
# Both entries are test request-id fixtures ("panic-req-456", "panic-test-789")
# passed as a context value. The generic-api-key rule scores them on entropy and
# the surrounding `Key: "value"` shape — right about the pattern, wrong about
# these two strings.
